xpandable-text-box">JinjaMonogatari =E2=80=93 Platform Development Update (=
Week 5)

Week 5 marks the end of mobile implementation until after the CMS has been =
completed. This week focused on persistence management, authentication stab=
ility, and improving overall usability.

JinjaMonogatari continues to evolve into a cultural exploration platform co=
mbining a mobile client, research CMS, and structured API architecture.

This week=E2=80=99s progress (API + Mobile):
Shrine Collection System:
- Completed full shrine bookmarking system with API endpoints and mobile in=
tegration
- Built a dedicated Collection screen
- Added global caching to keep saved shrines consistent across the app
Refresh Tokens &amp; Session Stability:
- Implemented refresh token rotation in the API
- Integrated token renewal and handling in mobile
- Improved logout handling to prevent stale or incorrect user state
Location &amp; Directions Improvements:
- Enabled real shrine distance calculations using PostGIS
- Direction buttons now lead to Google Maps when clicked
- Added multiple user location modes for testing and flexibility
Search &amp; Interaction Enhancements:
- Added search bar to Map, List, and Collection views
- Improved UI feedback (modals, button states, layout buffers)
- Expanded profile page with profile editing and theme selection
Architecture Improvements:
- Cleaned up API DTO contracts and handler structures
- Reorganized mobile folder structure for better separation of concerns

Key lessons
As I integrated features, managing data across screens and keeping sessions=
 stable became a headache, there were several times where I had to backtrac=
k to implement a better architectural decision for clarity and stronger sta=
te management.

Next focus
- Begin CMS planning and implementation
- Expand API alongside the CMS

As a user, the JinjaMonogatari application lets you discover Shinto shrines=
 across Japan through an interactive map, explore detailed cultural informa=
tion including history, kami, folklore, visual galleries, and etiquette gui=
dance to understand how to respectfully visit each location. You can search=
 for shrines, see distances from your location, get real-world directions, =
and save shrines to a personal collection tied to your account. The app com=
