" data-testid=3D"expandable-text-box">Status: Complete
Tech Stack: Angular, Tailwind CSS, ASP.NET Core Web API (CQRS, MediatR), Mo=
ngoDB

Project Overview:
A full-featured web catalog platform modeled after a fictional Japanese cra=
ft store. Built to reinforce real-world full-stack development practices wi=
th an emphasis on clean architecture, component reusability, and secure API=
 design. The system simulates two primary user roles ( shop owner (admin) a=
nd visitor (user) )with distinct access and responsibilities.

Architectural Decisions:
- CQRS + MediatR (Backend): Enables separation of concerns and scalable com=
mand/query handling.
- DTO Layer: Ensures controlled data exposure between client and server.
- Exception Middleware: Centralized for consistent API responses and cleane=
r logic.
- JWT Auth + Refresh Tokens: Secure token-based authentication with session=
 renewal strategy.
- Role-Based Access Control: API endpoints are protected via auth policies.
- Angular Routing + Guards: Restrict access to protected routes based on ro=
le and token presence.
- HTTP Interceptors: Centralized token injection and error handling.

Features:
Auth:
- JWT login system
- Role detection for conditional rendering
Product Catalog:
- Dynamic product card grid with responsive design
- Individual product pages with descriptions and image galleries
- Search, filter, and featured product sections
User Experience:
- Register/login flow
- Favorites page (user-specific saved items)
Admin Dashboard:
- Full CRUD for products
- Real-time metrics and product statistics

Purpose:
Built to gain experience with scalable architecture, secure authentication,=
 modular component design, and realistic frontend/backend workflows. The ap=
plication emphasizes maintainability, interactivity, and hands-on applicati=
on of full-stack concepts.<button class=3D"e65317de _578c35fa _5ba8eb7d _20=
